<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meerut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meerut is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, about 70 kilometres north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. On 10 May 1857 Indian sepoys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal-army">Bengal Army</a> mutinied in its cantonment after the punishment of soldiers who had refused the new greased cartridges, killed British officers and marched to Delhi, beginning the Indian Rebellion. Today it is a large commercial and industrial centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meerut.jpg" alt="Meerut" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MMKhan22 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mustafa_Castle_--_night_shot.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
